{"study_accession":"PRJNA690255","secondary_study_accession":"SRP300748","title":"Distinct B cell repertoires characterize patients with mild and severe COVID-19 [GEX]","description":"Protective immunity against COVID-19 likely depends on the production of SARS-CoV-2 binding plasma cells and memory B cells after infection or vaccination. Previous work has shown evidence that germinal center reactions, a critical component of the B cell response, are disrupted in severe COVID-19. This may adversely affect protective immunity from re-infection. Consistent with an extrafollicular B cell response, severe COVID-19 patients have large scale changes in B cell populations such as elevated frequencies of clonally expanded, class switched, unmutated plasmablasts. However, it is not clear whether mild or asymptomatically infected individuals show similar differences in B cell repertoires. Here, we use single cell RNA sequencing of B cells to show that, in contrast to hospitalized COVID-19 patients, mildly symptomatic COVID-19 subjects have B cell repertoires skewed towards clonally diverse, somatically hypermutated memory B cells approximately 30 days after the onset of symptoms. This provides evidence that B cell responses are less disrupted in mild COVID-19, and that the infection resolves with the production of memory B cells.  Overall design: Characterization of B cell response in mild symptomatic COVID-19 patients","pubmed":"34049971","geo_series":"","n_samples":11,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17248806","study_accession":"PRJNA690255","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"mild symptomatic COVID-19 donor, 201657036 (GEX)","description":"mild symptomatic COVID-19 donor, 201657036 (GEX)","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5008751","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-04-27","attributes":[["source_name","cryopreserved PBMCs"],["disease","mild symptomatic COVID-19"],["age","35"],["sex","male"],["time","33 days post symptom onset (DPSO)"],["cell_type","PBMCs"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13376433","experiment_accession":"SRX9799782","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":150523348,"base_count":12493437884,"first_public":"2021-04-27","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM5008751: mild symptomatic COVID-19 donor, 201657036 (GEX) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":true},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17248807","study_accession":"PRJNA690255","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"mild symptomatic COVID-19 donor, 201657034 (GEX)","description":"mild symptomatic COVID-19 donor, 201657034 (GEX)","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5008750","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-04-27","attributes":[["source_name","cryopreserved PBMCs"],["disease","mild symptomatic COVID-19"],["age","20"],["sex","male"],["time","24 days post symptom onset (DPSO)"],["cell_type","PBMCs"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13376432","experiment_accession":"SRX9799781","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":160419864,"base_count":13314848712,"first_public":"2021-04-27","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM5008750: mild symptomatic COVID-19 donor, 201657034 (GEX) Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":true},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17248808","study_accession":"PRJNA690255","blood_class":"pbmc","class_from":"sample","title":"Normal healthy donor, 2010113904 (GEX)","description":"Normal healthy donor, 2010113904 (GEX)","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5008749","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-04-27","attributes":[["source_name","cryopreserved PBMCs"],["disease","Normal healthy"],["age","23"],["sex","male"],["time","not applicable"],["cell_type","PBMCs"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13376431","experiment_accession":"SRX9799780","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrumen